## Invitations

- Table `business_invitations`: `business_id`, normalized `mobile`, `role` ∈ `{ADMIN,EDITOR,VIEWER}`, opaque `token`, `status`, `expires_at`, `invited_by_user_id`.
- Accept only after **OTP login** as that mobile (reuse Identity OTP — no separate invite OTP).
- Token links must not leak other businesses; accept checks mobile match + pending + not expired.
- One pending invite per `(businessId, mobile)`; revoke before re-invite with different role.

## Enforcement

- Nest: `@RequirePermission(...codes)` metadata + `EntitlementGuard` (membership permissions) **and** `@RequireWritable` / `@RequireModule` / `@RequireEntitlement` (subscription).
- `TenancyService.assertPermissions` / `assertPermission`.
- Fallback: writable routes without `@RequirePermission` still require EDITOR+ (`assertContentWriter`).
- UI mirrors `permissionsForRole(activeBusiness.role)`; API remains source of truth.
- `GET /api/businesses/:businessId/permissions` returns role + permission list.

## Audit

Append: `membership.invite`, `membership.accept`, `membership.role_change`, `membership.remove` (see `AuditActions`).
